1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,240
No water for his feet.

2
00:00:02,279 --> 00:00:02,939
No kiss.

3
00:00:04,159 --> 00:00:04,679
No oil.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,859
That's what Simon the Pharisee never gave

5
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,380
Jesus at his own table.

6
00:00:10,679 --> 00:00:12,399
A woman he hadn't invited walked in

7
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,619
anyway, and gave him all three.

8
00:00:15,979 --> 00:00:17,940
"A woman in the city, which was

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:18,500
a sinner...

10
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,899
brought an alabaster box of ointment, and

11
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,920
stood at his feet behind him weeping,

12
00:00:24,699 --> 00:00:26,279
and began to wash his feet with

13
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:26,920
tears...

14
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,899
and kissed his feet, and anointed them

15
00:00:30,959 --> 00:00:34,680
with the ointment." Simon thought it, not

16
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:35,180
out loud:

17
00:00:35,799 --> 00:00:37,819
"This man, if he were a prophet,

18
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:38,779
would have known...

19
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,099
for she is a sinner." Jesus answered

20
00:00:42,159 --> 00:00:42,619
anyway.

21
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:46,119
A creditor had two debtors — one

22
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:48,779
owed five hundred pence, one fifty.

23
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:51,079
"When they had nothing to pay, he

24
00:00:51,139 --> 00:00:53,819
frankly forgave them both" — frankly, that's

25
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:54,340
freely.

26
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:56,599
"Which of them will love him most?"

27
00:00:56,799 --> 00:00:57,559
Simon hedged:

28
00:00:58,079 --> 00:01:00,479
"I suppose that he, to whom he

29
00:01:00,539 --> 00:01:03,119
forgave most." Jesus turned to her, and

30
00:01:03,199 --> 00:01:04,360
asked Simon:

31
00:01:04,399 --> 00:01:06,719
"Seest thou this woman?" Simon had seen

32
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,339
the sin.

33
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:08,819
Never the woman.

34
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:11,580
"Her sins, which are many, are forgiven;

35
00:01:12,199 --> 00:01:13,299
for she loved much:

36
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:16,319
but to whom little is forgiven, the

37
00:01:16,379 --> 00:01:19,900
same loveth little." Forgiven first — love

38
00:01:19,939 --> 00:01:22,239
was the receipt, not the price.

39
00:01:23,939 --> 00:01:25,379
He turned from the parable to her:

40
00:01:25,879 --> 00:01:27,879
"Thy faith hath saved thee;

41
00:01:27,979 --> 00:01:30,019
go in peace." Not thy tears.

42
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:30,959
Not thy ointment.

43
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:32,279
Thy faith.

44
00:01:33,339 --> 00:01:35,239
That answer holds for whoever still carries

45
00:01:35,279 --> 00:01:37,419
what Simon called her — a sinner.

46
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:40,599
She came in carrying an alabaster box.

47
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,220
She left carrying his peace.
